## Article

```catala
declaration scope A:
    context output x content integer
    output o content integer

scope A:
    definition x equals 0
    definition x equals 1
    definition o equals 10
    exception definition o under condition x>0 consequence equals 20
```

The concolic interpreter tries different values for the context variable,
including the special "default" value. This allows for the detection of a
conflict when trying to compute the value in this case.

```catala-test-cli
$ catala Concolic --conc-optim=incremental -s A
┌─[WARNING]─
│
│  Multiple conflicting definitions:
│  these have the same conditions and will always trigger a conflict at runtime.
│
├─➤ tests/concolic/good/context_conflict_on_default.catala_en:9.16-17:
│   │
│ 9 │     definition x equals 0
│   │                ‾
├─ Article
│
├─➤ tests/concolic/good/context_conflict_on_default.catala_en:10.16-17:
│    │
│ 10 │     definition x equals 1
│    │                ‾
└─ Article
┌─[WARNING]─
│
│  Output of scope after evaluation:
│    ↯Conflict↯ at context_conflict_on_default:5.20-21
│      This consequence has a valid justification:
│      ─➤ tests/concolic/good/context_conflict_on_default.catala_en:9.25-26:
│        │
│      9 │     definition x equals 0
│        │                         ‾
│      Article
│      This consequence has a valid justification:
│      ─➤ tests/concolic/good/context_conflict_on_default.catala_en:10.25-26:
│         │
│      10 │     definition x equals 1
│         │                         ‾
│      Article
│
└─
┌─[RESULT]─ Concolic execution ─
│ Executed 3 tests:
│     Inputs │ Outputs
│ ────── Test #1 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
│ x_in = ⟨0⟩ │ x = 0
│            │ o = 10
│ ────── Test #2 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
│ x_in = ⟨1⟩ │ x = 1
│            │ o = 20
│ ────── Test #3 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
│ x_in = ∅   │ ↯Conflict↯ at context_conflict_on_default:5.20-21
│            │   This consequence has a valid justification:
│            │   ─➤ tests/concolic/good/context_conflict_on_default.catala_en:9.25-26:
│            │     │
│            │   9 │     definition x equals 0
│            │     │                         ‾
│            │   Article
│            │   This consequence has a valid justification:
│            │   ─➤ tests/concolic/good/context_conflict_on_default.catala_en:10.25-26:
│            │      │
│            │   10 │     definition x equals 1
│            │      │                         ‾
│            │   Article
└─
```

